          "date": "2026-10-13 06:18:16.000000000",
          "tz": 180
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Alexey Lyashkov",
          "email": "alexey.lyashkov@hpe.com",
          "date": "2026-10-13 07:41:49.000000000",
          "tz": 180
        },
        "subject": "LU-20943 lnet: fix off by one in recovery key list alloc",
        "message": "LU-20943 lnet: fix off by one in recovery key list alloc\n\nlnet_debug_recovery_show_dump() builds a dynamic ln_key_list to\ndescribe the NIDs currently sitting in a recovery queue. The number\nof keys is computed as:\n\n        count = debug_recovery_attr_list.lkl_maxattr +\n                drlist->lgdrl_count - 1;\n\nbut the buffer for the flexible lkl_list[] array was sized for only\n'count' entries. The key list is indexed by the netlink attribute\nnumber, which starts at 1 (index 0 is the unused *_ATTR_UNSPEC slot),\nso valid entries run from 0 to lkl_maxattr inclusive and 'count + 1'\nelements are required.\n\nAs a result, filling in the last \"nid-N\" key and later walking the\nlist in lnet_genl_parse_list() touch one ln_key_props past the end of\nthe allocation, which KASAN reports as a slab-out-of-bounds write and\nwhich can panic the node:\n\n BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in lnet_debug_recovery_show_dump\n Write of size 8 at addr ffff88810489e828 by task lt-lnetctl\n\nHit by sanity-lnet test_210 and test_211 ('lnetctl debug recovery').\n\nAllocate room for 'count + 1' key properties so the whole index range\nis backed by the allocation.\n\nHPe-bug-id: LUS-13538\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet\nSigned-off-by: Alexey Lyashkov <alexey.lyashkov@hpe.com>\nChange-Id: Ia245967625f11311ddebb6fc704055ff819e6be5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
